.\"	$GergiOS: mac-compile.8,v 1.0 2026/07/10 $
.\"
.Dd July 10, 2026
.Dt MAC-COMPILE 8
.Os GergiOS
.Sh NAME
.Nm mac-compile
.Nd compile MAC policy rules into binary format
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl o Ar output
.Op Fl v
.Op Ar input_file
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility reads MAC policy rules in human-readable format
from
.Ar input_file
(or stdin) and compiles them into a compact binary format
that the MAC policy daemon
.Xr macd 8
can load quickly at startup.
.Pp
The compiled policy is significantly faster to load because
.Xr macd 8
does not need to re-parse text or resolve service labels at
startup time.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl o Ar output
Write compiled policy to
.Ar output
instead of stdout.
.It Fl v
Verbose mode: print a summary of the number of rules compiled
and the output size.
.It Fl h
Show usage summary.
.El
.Sh INPUT FORMAT
The input format is identical to
.Pa /etc/macd.conf :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# This is a comment
<allow|deny> <op> [from <label>] [to <label>]
.Ed
.Pp
Supported operations:
.Bl -column "PRIVCTL_SET_SYS" "Description" -offset indent
.It Sy Op Ta Sy Description
.It ALL      Ta Matches all operations
.It IPC_SEND Ta IPC send
.It IPC_RECEIVE Ta IPC receive
.It FILE_ACCESS Ta File access (open/read/write/execute)
.It PRIVCTL_SET_SYS Ta Setting system privileges
.It DEVICE_BIND Ta Device driver binding
.It PROC_FORK Ta Process fork
.It PROC_EXEC Ta Process exec
.It PROC_KILL Ta Signal delivery
.It RAWIO    Ta Raw I/O access
.El
.Pp
Labels are service names from
.Pa /etc/system.conf
(e.g., vfs, pm, rs, init).
The special label
.Sy ANY
matches all endpoints.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/macd.policy -compact
.It Pa /etc/macd.conf
Default text-format policy file.
.It Pa /etc/macd.policy
Default binary-format policy file (compiled output).
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Compile the default policy:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
mac-compile -o /etc/macd.policy /etc/macd.conf
.Ed
.Pp
Validate a policy file without writing output (check for errors):
.Bd -literal -offset indent
mac-compile /etc/macd.conf > /dev/null
.Ed
.Pp
Compile with verbose output:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
mac-compile -v -o /etc/macd.policy /etc/macd.conf
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr macd 8 ,
.Xr macd.conf 5 ,
.Xr mac-compile 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
command first appeared in GergiOS 1.0.
